00:14:10.079 --> 00:14:14.720
It'll rebuild some of the parts. When

00:14:12.399 --> 00:14:17.760
it's ready, I click on it. I check it

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:21.279
out. Nice. It's working. Now you have

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:24.320
started inching toward your own

00:14:21.279 --> 00:14:26.800
relationship management system. It's not

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:29.680
a spreadsheet anymore. It's how you keep

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:33.120
in touch with those who are close to

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:35.760
you, those in your closest orbit. And

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:38.720
now we go to the final step. E for

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:41.279
evolve. The final step is not just to

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:44.240
evolve what you build, but to make sure

00:14:41.279 --> 00:14:48.160
you evolve with it. Anthropic did a

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:50.880
study that looked at roughly 400,000

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:53.600
real sessions of people building

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:56.800
software apps with AI. And the results

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:59.360
were surprising. They found that people

00:14:56.800 --> 00:15:03.040
who had never programmed before

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:06.320
succeeded almost as often as trained

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:08.240
engineers and managers actually scored

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:11.199
slightly higher than even software

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:15.120
engineers. Now, it was just a survey and

00:15:11.199 --> 00:15:17.839
not a super rigorous study, but it does

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:20.800
point to an interesting fact. The whole

00:15:17.839 --> 00:15:24.079
skill of vibe coding boils down to

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:28.079
knowing what you want and describing it

00:15:24.079 --> 00:15:31.440
clearly to your staff, which is your AI

00:15:28.079 --> 00:15:36.160
coder in this case. So, the best people

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:39.120
managers become the best AI managers. So

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:42.399
from here you can evolve in three

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:45.920
different directions. First, the app you

00:15:42.399 --> 00:15:49.600
build can evolve into a a system. You

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:52.320
can reuse the code to make a CRM for

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:55.759
your side hustle, a tracker for your

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:59.360
kids soccer team, a dashboard for your

00:15:55.759 --> 00:16:02.079
goals, whatever comes to mind. Second,

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:05.759
if you feel like it, you can go a bit

00:16:02.079 --> 00:16:08.560
deeper. You can learn about APIs and how

00:16:05.759 --> 00:16:12.240
to connect with other apps, how to use

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:14.399
GitHub, and what those Python libraries

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:17.440
actually do. And every time you get

00:16:14.399 --> 00:16:20.639
stuck, don't be afraid to ask clarifying

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:23.199
questions. Open Claw Chat or any chat

00:16:20.639 --> 00:16:26.000
and ask it to explain it like you are a

00:16:23.199 --> 00:16:29.199
10year-old. And the third direction is

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:33.279
try to learn something about coding.

00:16:29.199 --> 00:16:36.079
Even if your career right now has almost

00:16:33.279 --> 00:16:39.199
nothing to do with software because of

00:16:36.079 --> 00:16:41.839
all the things AI will change, software

00:16:39.199 --> 00:16:44.480
building is one of the areas where AI

00:16:41.839 --> 00:16:46.320
will improve incredibly quickly in the

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:49.519
coming years. And there are reasons for

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:52.639
that. But that also means that anyone

00:16:49.519 --> 00:16:55.759
with the right tools can create absolute

00:16:52.639 --> 00:16:57.920
magic. The world is still going to need

00:16:55.759 --> 00:17:00.959
great software engineers to understand

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:05.039
complex systems and architectures and

00:17:00.959 --> 00:17:07.360
security and much more. But this new way

00:17:05.039 --> 00:17:10.720
of working and building your digital

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:14.079
life is coming at you at 100 miles an

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:18.240
hour. So spend a weekend tinkering with

00:17:14.079 --> 00:17:21.039
claude code or lovable or replet or

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:24.559
maybe take an online course because the

00:17:21.039 --> 00:17:27.919
real goal is to become comfortable

00:17:24.559 --> 00:17:31.520
building, breaking and rebuilding

00:17:27.919 --> 00:17:35.840
things. What you build today will tell

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:39.039
you what to build next. So go ahead and

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:41.600
make a bad version.

00:17:39.039 --> 00:17:43.760
That's the only way you'll know how to

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:48.240
make the best one.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:48.240
Thank you and I love you.

